{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"ffbab5f3-f63e-41a6-9d1d-4757b045db89","step_index":14,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.432174,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"aws s3 sync help"},"output":"\u003ctruncated 459 lines\u003e\n       files t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains\r\n       no objects.\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test.txt\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 2\b2:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl S\bS3\b3 o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs f\bfr\bro\bom\bm t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd S\bS3\b3 b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt t\bto\bo a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br\r\n       b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs objects under a specified prefix and\r\n       bucket to objects under another specified prefix and bucket by copying\r\n       S3 objects. An S3 object will require copying if the sizes of the two\r\n       S3 objects differ, the last modified time of the source is newer than\r\n       the last modified time of the destination, or the S3 object does not\r\n       exist under the specified bucket and prefix destination.\r\n\r\n       In this example, the user syncs the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt to the\r\n       bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt2\b2. The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains\r\n       the objects t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt. The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt2\b2\r\n       contains no objects:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket2\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          copy: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket2/test.txt\r\n          copy: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket2/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 3\b3:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl S\bS3\b3 o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs f\bfr\bro\bom\bm t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd S\bS3\b3 b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be\r\n       l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl d\bdi\bir\bre\bec\bct\bto\bor\bry\by\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs files from the specified S3 bucket to\r\n       the local directory by downloading S3 objects. An S3 object will\r\n       require downloading if the size of the S3 object differs from the size\r\n       of the local file, the last modified time of the S3 object is newer\r\n       than the last modified time of the local file, or the S3 object does\r\n       not exist in the local directory. Take note that when objects are\r\n       downloaded from S3, the last modified time of the local file is changed\r\n       to the last modified time of the S3 object. In this example, the user\r\n       syncs the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt to the current local directory.\r\n       The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains the objects t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The current local directory has no files:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket .\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          download: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test.txt to test.txt\r\n          download: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt to test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 4\b4:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt a\ban\bnd\bd d\bde\bel\ble\bet\bte\be\r\n       a\bal\bll\bl f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs t\bth\bha\bat\bt d\bdo\bo n\bno\bot\bt m\bma\bat\btc\bch\bh\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs objects under a specified prefix and\r\n       bucket to files in a local directory by uploading the local files to\r\n       S3.  Because of the -\b--\b-d\bde\bel\ble\bet\bte\be parameter, any files existing under the\r\n       specified prefix and bucket but not existing in the local directory\r\n       will be deleted.  In this example, the user syncs the bucket\r\n       a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt to the local current directory.  The local current\r\n       directory contains the files t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket\r\n       a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains the object t\bte\bes\bst\bt3\b3.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket \\\r\n              --delete\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test.txt\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test3.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 5\b5:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt\r\n       `\b``\b`.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg`\b``\b` f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs objects under a specified prefix and\r\n       bucket to files in a local directory by uploading the local files to\r\n       S3. Because of the -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter, all files matching the pattern\r\n       existing both in S3 and locally will be excluded from the sync. In this\r\n       example, the user syncs the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt to the local\r\n       current directory.  The local current directory contains the files\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains the\r\n       object t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg of a different size than the local t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket \\\r\n              --exclude \"*.jpg\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 6\b6:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt\r\n       s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd d\bdi\bir\bre\bec\bct\bto\bor\bry\by f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs files under a local directory to\r\n       objects under a specified prefix and bucket by downloading S3 objects.\r\n       This example uses the -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter flag to exclude a specified\r\n       directory and S3 prefix from the s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command.  In this example, the\r\n       user syncs the local current directory to the bucket\r\n       a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt.  The local current directory contains the files\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br/\b/t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt\r\n       contains the objects a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br/\b/t\bte\bes\bst\bt5\b5.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt1\b1.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/ . \\\r\n              --exclude \"*another/*\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          download: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test1.txt to test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 7\b7:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs b\bbe\bet\btw\bwe\bee\ben\bn b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bts\bs i\bin\bn d\bdi\bif\bff\bfe\ber\bre\ben\bnt\bt r\bre\beg\bgi\bio\bon\bns\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs files between two buckets in different\r\n       regions:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://my-us-west-2-bucket s3://my-us-east-1-bucket \\\r\n              --source-region us-west-2 \\\r\n              --region us-east-1\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          download: s3://my-us-west-2-bucket/test1.txt to s3://my-us-east-1-bucket/test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 8\b8:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc t\bto\bo a\ban\bn S\bS3\b3 a\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bs p\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs the current directory to the access\r\n       point (m\bmy\bya\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bsp\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt):\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test.txt to s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/test.txt\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/test2.txt\r\n\r\n                                                                        SYNC()\r\n"}}}
