{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"ffbab5f3-f63e-41a6-9d1d-4757b045db89","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the deployment configuration to add appropriate `Cache-Control` headers and documented the changes in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-M9nEzj/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[`scripts/deploy.sh`](file:///tmp/h-M9nEzj/scripts/deploy.sh)**:\n   - Added `aws s3 sync` for `src/assets/` using `--cache-control \"public, max-age=31536000, immutable\"` for long-term caching of static images and media.\n   - Added `aws s3 sync` for `src/` (excluding `assets/*`) using `--cache-control \"public, max-age=0, must-revalidate\"` so browsers revalidate HTML and JavaScript files (`booking.js`) on every visit without holding stale versions for days.\n2. **[ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-M9nEzj/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Documented the rationale and specific cache directives configured for each file category.\n","duration_seconds":51.104479,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":130081,"output_tokens":1782,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":126114,"total_tokens":131863}}}
